HighestWeights -- decompose free resolutions and graded modules with a semisimple Lie group action
**************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

This package provides tools to study the representation theoretic structure of
equivariant free resolutions and graded modules with the action of a semisimple
Lie group. The methods of this package allow one to consider the free modules
in an equivariant resolution, or the graded components of a module, as
representations of a semisimple Lie group by means of their weights and to
obtain their decomposition into highest weight representations.

This package implements an algorithm introduced in Galetto - Propagating
weights of tori along free resolutions (see
http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.jsc.2015.05.004 ). The methods of this package are
meant to be used in characteristic zero.

The following links contain some sample computations carried out using this
package. The first and second example are discussed in more detail, so we
recommend reading through them first.

  * *note Example 1: Example 1, -- The coordinate ring of the Grassmannian
  * *note Example 2: Example 2, -- The Buchsbaum-Rim complex
  * *note Example 3: Example 3, -- A multigraded Eagon-Northcott complex
  * *note Example 4: Example 4, -- The Eisenbud-Fløystad-Weyman complex
  * *note Example 5: Example 5, -- The singular locus of a symplectic invariant
  * *note Example 6: Example 6, -- The coordinate ring of the spinor variety
  * *note Example 7: Example 7, -- With the exceptional group G2

